d7768bdb01941d87c283e4f92adca628ec9a90fc51e40ea69db9fb4f3", "text": "After leaving Liverpool, Klopp was asked about the possibility of receiving titles retrospectively. At his January 2025 Red Bull appearance, he joked about a celebration at his Mallorca home. He said that if it happened, he would book a flight, buy the beer, and hold a parade in his garden. Supporters immediately understood the joke. They remembered how close Liverpool came. The idea of celebrating years later turned a complicated case into something instantly recognisable. But a joke is not a decision. The financial conduct described in the Premier League's published findings covers 2009/10 to 2017/18. Liverpool's runner-up seasons under Klopp came later. The argument about a squad built over time may matter to the debate. It does not establish that either of those later titles must be reassigned. The sanction and appeal process has to answer its own questions.", "voice_id": "bu5eKETbFKC8G702EAU4", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2"}